.TH READ 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
read \- read bytes from a file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t read(int " descriptor ", void* " buffer ", size_t " byte_count ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR read ()
requests up to
.I byte_count
bytes from
.I descriptor
into
.IR buffer .
The caller must provide enough writable storage for the count.
The function does not append a NUL byte or check the buffer capacity.
.PP
Short reads are possible. A call interrupted before transferring data is
reported as an error; this wrapper does not retry automatically.
.B STDIN_FILENO
in
.B <unistd.h>
names the standard input descriptor.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the number of bytes read is returned; zero can indicate end of
file, or a zero\-length request.
On failure, \-1 is returned and
.B errno
is set to the positive Linux error number.
Successful calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.B <errno.h>
to inspect
.BR errno .
Possible errors include
.BR EBADF ,
.BR EFAULT ,
.BR EAGAIN ,
and
.BR EINTR ;
other Linux
.BR read (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
This Crunch function uses the Linux x86\-64 syscall and is linked from
.BR libcrunch.a .
Its
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch),
.BR lseek (3crunch),
.BR input (3crunch),
.BR read (2)
